  /* Film lies on the paper like real film with no light behind it: solid, so a roll on top simply covers the ones
     under it, photos included, and a pile is one grey however many layers deep. (It used to be see-through, multiplied
     over whatever lay under it, and every crossing made a new, darker shape.) */
