  @keyframes fall { from { opacity: 0; translate: 0 -9vh; scale: 1.16; rotate: var(--spin, 12deg); } }
  /* A lifted roll (hovered, or tapped once on a touch screen) is a little larger and turns silver: the film's own
     colour, solid, with nothing under it showing through.
     The silver is a copy of the film in the photo layer, shown in place of the real film, which is hidden. The real
     film grows and shrinks with the photo layer, so when it comes back on letting go the two are the same size and
     settle together. (It used to stay put, and the photos visibly slid across it for the 0.7s they took to shrink.)
